    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct membership-level rule with a points system.\n\n**What changed:**\n\n1. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Replaced the old `membershipLevel` computation (level started at 1, +1 per factor, capped at 4) with:\n   - `membershipPoints(owner)`: starts at 0, **+2** email present, **+1** `namesakeCount == 0`, **+2** household of 3+, **+3** tenure over 365 days.\n   - `membershipLevel(owner)`: maps points \u2192 level: 1 (0\u20131), 2 (2\u20133), 3 (4\u20135), 4 (6+).\n   - `householdSize(owner)`: counts owners sharing the stored `householdId` (an owner with no `householdId` counts as just itself). This required injecting `OwnerRepository` into the mapper (`@Autowired protected` field), consistent with how `AssignOwnerNamesakeCount` counts via the repository. The mapper is a Spring component (`mapstruct.defaultComponentModel=spring`), so injection works.\n   - Both fields are emitted via `@Mapping` expressions.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the new `membershipPoints` response field (read-only, min 0) and updated `membershipLevel` (now 1\u20134, new description). The `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec, so the `membershipPoints` property is generated automatically.\n\n**Verification:** The `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsPointsAndLevel` case (email + no namesake, single-member household, zero tenure \u2192 3 points \u2192 level 2) passes, and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nOne design note worth flagging: household size and tenure are computed live at read time (as tenure always was), so `membershipPoints`/`membershipLevel` can change on later GETs as an owner's household grows or it crosses 365 days \u2014 they are not frozen at creation. The household count is done via `findAll()` per owner mapped, which is fine at this scale but is O(n) per owner on list endpoints.",
