    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of what happens on `POST /api/owners` (full external route `POST /petclinic/api/owners`, guarded by `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`; the entire pipeline runs under `govern: [ transaction ]`).\n\nSteps in the YAML run strictly in `next:` order. Below, **[V]** = validation (can reject the request), **[S]** = side-effect/mutation.\n\n### Up front (before the pipeline)\n- **[V] Authorization** \u2014 caller must hold role `OWNER_ADMIN`, else `AuthorizationDeniedException`.\n- **[V] Bean validation** on `OwnerFieldsDto` *if OfficeFloor bean-validation is wired* \u2014 `@NotNull`/`@Size`/`@Pattern` on firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone (digits-only), email size. (The pipeline re-checks most of this in code regardless.)\n\n### Pipeline (in order)\n1. **normalizeAddress** \u2014 **[S]** reads the request body once; normalizes `address` (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE`); republishes the DTO for later steps.\n2. **require** \u2014 **[V]** rejects if any of firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone is null/blank \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400, lists missing fields). Runs *after* normalize, so a blank-after-normalization address is caught here.\n3. **validatePostcode** \u2014 **[V]** if postcode present, must be 4 digits; if the city maps to a known region, must fall in that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (400). Blank postcode is allowed.\n4. **validateRegistrationDate** \u2014 **[V]** if `registrationDate` is after today, reject \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400).\n5. **normalize** (telephone) \u2014 **[V]+[S]** strips spaces/dashes/parens, applies `+61` default (dropping a leading 0) unless it starts with `+`, checks E.164 shape and per-country national-number length, and **writes back** the normalized `+<digits>` telephone \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400).\n6. **normalizeEmail** \u2014 **[V]+[S]** if email present, lower-cases it, validates a basic email regex, **writes it back** \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` (400). Blank email allowed.\n7. **rejectDisposableEmail** \u2014 **[V]** if email present, rejects domains `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com` \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException` (400).\n8. **checkIdentity** \u2014 **[V]** scans all owners; rejects if the identity key (telephone|email|householdId) already exists, or (unless `sharesHousehold` is true) if the household id already exists \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409).\n9. **checkCityCapacity** \u2014 **[V]** rejects if the normalized city already has \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n10. **checkDailyLimit** \u2014 **[V]** rejects if \u2265 100 owners are already registered for today's business day \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (429). (Ignores the request body.)\n11. **build** \u2014 **[S]** maps the DTO into a new `Owner` entity (via `OwnerMapper`, ignoring id/pets); publishes it.\n12. **assignHousehold** \u2014 **[S]** sets `householdId` (hash of lastName|postcode).\n13. **defaultRegistrationDate** \u2014 **[S]** defaults `registrationDate` to today if null, then rolls weekend dates forward to Monday (business day).\n14. **assignCustomerCode** \u2014 **[S]** sets `customerCode` = `<region>-<8-char SHA-256 hash of telephone+lastName>`.\n15. **assignMembershipNumber** \u2014 **[S]** sets `membershipNumber` = `<customerCode>-M<yy>` from the registration year.\n16. **assignNamesakeCount** \u2014 **[S]** sets `namesakeCount` = count of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive; excludes the new one since it's pre-save).\n17. **assignPossibleDuplicate** \u2014 **[S]** sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`: defaults false/null; if not sharing a household and postcode present, flags a duplicate when an existing owner shares last name + postcode but has a different telephone.\n18. **save** \u2014 **[S]** persists the owner via `OwnerRepository.save`. A DB constraint failure surfaces as `DataIntegrityViolationException` (handled as **404** \u2014 note that unusual status) or otherwise the generic 500 handler.\n19. **audit** \u2014 **[S]** logs to the `AUDIT` SLF4J logger: `owner created id=\u2026 customerCode=\u2026 registrationDate=\u2026`.\n20. **respond** \u2014 **[S]** maps to `OwnerDto`, sets `bulkSignupWarning` (true when today's registrations exceed 80), and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n### Notes worth flagging\n- The whole pipeline is one transaction (`govern: [ transaction ]` on every step), committed once at the end \u2014 so all side-effects (including the save) roll back together if a later step throws.\n- Entity-level constraints also apply at persist time: `Owner` requires E.164 telephone (`^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$`), non-empty address/city, and `Person` requires non-empty first/last name \u2014 these back up the in-code checks.\n- `checkDailyLimit` counts against today's *business day* (weekends roll forward), matching the date actually assigned in step 13.\n\nI did not modify anything."
